  ],
  "ci": "distribution-free order-statistic interval: the binomial ranks of the quantile, so no density or symmetry assumption enters the bound",
  "se": "spacing estimator f(q) = (k2-k1)/(n*(x_k2-x_k1)) with k = n*q +- sqrt(n*q*(1-q)), SE = sqrt(q(1-q)/n)/f -- published as the second, density-based reading of the same width",
  "perm": "pooled-label permutation of the two arms' rows; statistic = difference of the sample quantile. Null = the block length does not change the resampled distribution, which is exactly what the ladder claims to test. Note it is a whole-distribution null, so a difference anywhere shows up here",
  "pairs": "each arm against the iid arm (block 1) plus each ladder neighbour",
  "resolve_rule": "n_needed = n * (z * se_diff / gap)^2, z = 1.96 (E162 reader-horizon law applied to a quantile rather than to a t-test)",
  "frozen": "constants written before the first run; the gate re-derives from rows"
